// Cloudflare Pages: assets-only deployment.
//
// The docs site is fully static (Astro Starlight, `output: "static"`,
// no SSR adapter). Wrangler uploads the prerendered `dist/` directory
// straight to Cloudflare's edge.
//
// Three fields are deliberately absent compared to a Workers-style
// config:
//
//   - `main`: no Worker entrypoint. Astro doesn't emit `dist/_worker.js`
//     when there's no adapter, and wrangler rejects a `main` that
//     points to a missing file.
//   - `compatibility_flags` (`nodejs_compat`, `global_fetch_strictly_public`):
//     only meaningful for a Worker runtime. Static assets don't run
//     Node code on the edge.
//   - `assets.binding`: only valid when a Worker reads the bundled
//     assets via the ASSETS binding at runtime. Wrangler refuses
//     `assets.binding` without a corresponding `main`.
//
// If/when we add an edge Worker (e.g. for OG-image generation), bring
// these fields back together with the adapter.
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "boring-stack-landing-page",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-05-13",
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "assets": {
    "directory": "dist"
  }
}
